// Pure-state vector representation.
// State after K gates is a vector in C^{2^n}.
//   |psi_0> in C^{2^n}
//   for k in 1..K:
//       |psi_k> = U_k |psi_{k-1}>
//   p(i) = |<i|psi_K>|^2
// Storage: 2 * 2^n real numbers; gate application is one matrix-vector mult, O(4^n) but
// often structured (sparse or block-Kronecker) to give O(2^n) per gate.
circuit StateVector(n, U_1, ..., U_K, |psi_0>):
    state := |psi_0>
    for k in 1..K:
        state := U_k * state
    return state, measurement_probabilities = |<i|state>|^2 for i = 0..2^n - 1

target_form:
// Density-matrix representation.
// State is a 2^n by 2^n complex matrix; for a pure state it has rank 1.
//   rho_0 = |psi_0><psi_0|
//   for k in 1..K:
//       rho_k = U_k * rho_{k-1} * U_k^*
//   p(i) = <i|rho_K|i>
// Storage: 4^n complex numbers (worst case). Conjugation by U_k is two
// matrix-matrix multiplications, O(8^n) naive or O(4^n) for structured U_k.
// Use case: expressing decoherence channels rho -> sum_k K_k rho K_k^* with Kraus
// operators K_k (not a single unitary), partial-tracing over an environment, or
// tracking mixed states from probabilistic preparation.
circuit DensityMatrix(n, U_1, ..., U_K, |psi_0>):
    rho := |psi_0><psi_0|
    for k in 1..K:
        rho := U_k * rho * U_k^*
    return rho, measurement_probabilities = <i|rho|i> for i = 0..2^n - 1

