// Standard Grover with k iterations of (Oracle * Diffusion):
//   |s> = H^{tensor n} |0>^n            // uniform superposition
//   repeat k times:
//       apply Oracle_marked         // |x> -> (-1)^{f(x)} |x>
//       apply 2|s><s| - I           // diffusion about |s>
//   measure -> outcome x with f(x)=1 w.p. ~ sin^2((2k+1)*theta), theta=arcsin(sqrt(M/N))
// Optimal k = round((pi/4)*sqrt(N/M)) gives success >~ 1 - M/N; OVERSHOOTING causes oscillation.
circuit Grover_standard(N, M, k):
    prepare |s> = H^{tensor n}|0>^n
    for i in 1..k:
        apply Oracle_marked
        apply Diffusion = (2|s><s| - I)
    return measure(state)

