// Fixed-point Grover (Yoder-Low-Chuang 2014). Replace the phase-pi oracle with a sequence of
// L phase-rotations {alpha_1,...,alpha_L} and the corresponding diffusion phases {beta_l},
// chosen so that the polynomial response in sin(theta) is the (1-T_L(x)/T_L(1))/2 polynomial
// (Chebyshev of degree L). Success probability is monotone in L; saturates at >= 1 - delta^L
// for any delta in (0,1). Total query count L = O(log(1/epsilon)/(2*theta)) = O(sqrt(N/M)*log(1/epsilon)).
circuit Grover_fixed_point(N, M, epsilon):
    L := smallest integer with 1 - (delta)^L >= 1 - epsilon, where delta is chosen <1
    {alpha_l, beta_l} := optimal_phase_schedule(L)   // Yoder-Low-Chuang formula
    prepare |s> = H^{tensor n}|0>^n
    for l in 1..L:
        apply Generalized_Oracle(alpha_l)
        apply Generalized_Diffusion(beta_l)
    return measure(state)

